Subject: [PATCH] toolkit: default page icon is the Aequera mark

Why Firefox source must change:
  The fallback page icon (chrome://global/skin/icons/defaultFavicon.svg,
  FAVICON_DEFAULT_URL in toolkit/components/places/nsIFaviconService.idl)
  is a Mozilla globe baked into toolkit's shared skin. No build option,
  branding directory, or preference redirects it: the URL is part of the
  favicon-service contract and is referenced across browser/toolkit chrome
  (tabs, address bar, library, prompts, page-icon protocol). Reaching it
  requires changing the upstream file.

What it changes (1 file, no behavior of its own):
  - toolkit/themes/shared/icons/defaultFavicon.svg: globe -> Aequera
    geometric mark, same construction as
    aequera/design/branding/source/aequera-icon.svg (one congruent
    three-face block, exact 120-degree rotations about (205,214), faces
    #4ED5FF/#4EFFFF). Fixed brand fills replace context-fill so the mark
    reads as product identity in light and dark contexts; the proton/nova
    variant switch goes away with the globe. URL, file name, and packaging
    (toolkit/themes/shared/desktop-jar.inc.mn) are unchanged.

Depends on: none. Touches a unique file; independent of other series.
Validation: `aequera patch status` (applied state matches manifest);
  artifact build + run: chrome://global/skin/icons/defaultFavicon.svg
  renders the mark, and a favicon-less page shows it in the tab strip.
  places favicon tests reference only the URL spec, which is unchanged.
Upstream risk: low. Conflicts only if Mozilla redesigns the globe; the
  file is otherwise stable for long stretches.

diff --git a/toolkit/themes/shared/icons/defaultFavicon.svg b/toolkit/themes/shared/icons/defaultFavicon.svg
index 46ccd0fe6c0e..40f89f1c8995 100644
--- a/toolkit/themes/shared/icons/defaultFavicon.svg
+++ b/toolkit/themes/shared/icons/defaultFavicon.svg
@@ -1,19 +1,44 @@
